the cell above is 7: when the right neighbour is 7 or off the grid, paint 6 and stop. Otherwise paint the current cell 4, turn the 7 above into 8, and step right.\n  - Otherwise paint 2 and step up.\n- **Going right at (y,x):**\n  - If the cell above is 7, paint 2. If the next cell to the right is blocked (a 7 or off the grid), paint 6 and stop; otherwise keep moving right.\n  - If the cell above is not 7, paint 3 and switch to going up.\n\n**Teaching stages:** I emit one canvas after each complete path from a 6 marker, then the final grid.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid).copy()\n    H, W = g.shape\n    starts = [x for x in range(W) if g[H-1, x] == 6]\n    for sx in starts:\n        y, x = H - 2, sx\n        mode = 'up'\n        steps = 0\n        while steps < 4 * H * W:\n            steps += 1\n            if mode == 'up':\n                if y == 0:\n                    g[y, x] = 6\n                    break\n                if g[y-1, x] == 7:\n                    if x + 1 >= W or g[y, x+1] == 7:\n                        g[y, x] = 6\n                        break\n                    g[y, x] = 4\n                    g[y-1, x] = 8\n                    x += 1\n                    mode = 'right'\n                else:\n                    g[y, x] = 2\n                    y -= 1\n            else:\n                if y > 0 and g[y-1, x] in (7, 8):\n                    if x + 1 >= W or g[y, x+1] == 7:\n                        g[y, x] = 6\n                        break\n                    g[y, x] = 2\n                    x += 1\n                else:\n                    g[y, x] = 3\n                    y -= 1\n                    mode = 'up'\n                    if y < 0:\n                        break\n        emit(g, f\"Traced the path launched by the 6 at bottom column {sx}: climb (2), \"\n                f\"turn under a 7 bar (4 corner, 7->8), slide right (2), climb again at the bar's end (3), \"\n                f\"ending in 6 at the top or when boxed in.\")\n    emit(g, \"All paths drawn; final grid.\")\n    return g\n","candidate_tactics":{"movement":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"When a 7 blocks it, the path slides right underneath that 7 bar and then resumes climbing."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"aced the path launched by the 6 at bottom column 4: climb (2), turn under a 7 bar (4 corner, 7->8), slide right (2), climb again at the bar's end (3), ending in 6 at the top or when boxed in."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"aced the path launched by the 6 at bottom column 8: climb (2), turn under a 7 bar (4 corner, 7->8), slide right (2), climb again at the bar's end (3), ending in 6 at the top or when boxed in."}],"paths":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Comparing inputs and outputs shows that each 6 launches a path that climbs upward."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"When a 7 blocks it, the path slides right underneath that 7 bar and then resumes climbing."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"The path cell becomes 4 (the turn corner) and the 7 it bumped into becomes 8."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"b35aa6721c58d89f3c4f4bb78db0bb2b79abc2ab738bad84e7bcb68d9f266d4e","task_sha256":"2c7d7e23710958143284d93f904853b8746b7b349a8cdb9f77b15bd3333856cd","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
